# What Debian calls the things profiles ask for.
#
# Many of these are genuine Debian virtual packages, in which case the
# alias is redundant and harmless: expansion keeps the original name
# first, so the real capability wins.

Capability: web-browser
Resolves-To: firefox | firefox-esr | chromium | epiphany-browser

Capability: terminal-emulator
Resolves-To: x-terminal-emulator | konsole | gnome-terminal | xterm

Capability: file-manager
Resolves-To: dolphin | nautilus | thunar | pcmanfm

Capability: text-editor
Resolves-To: editor | kate | gedit | nano

Capability: document-viewer
Resolves-To: evince | okular | atril

Capability: image-viewer
Resolves-To: eog | gwenview | ristretto

Capability: word-processor
Resolves-To: libreoffice-writer | abiword

Capability: spreadsheet
Resolves-To: libreoffice-calc | gnumeric

Capability: mail-transport-agent
Resolves-To: postfix | exim4-daemon-light | nullmailer | msmtp-mta

Capability: audio-server
Resolves-To: pipewire | pulseaudio

Capability: vulkan-driver
Resolves-To: mesa-vulkan-drivers | nvidia-driver-libs

Capability: opengl
Resolves-To: libgl1 | libgl1-mesa-glx

Capability: firewall
Resolves-To: ufw | nftables | iptables

Capability: time-sync
Resolves-To: systemd-timesyncd | chrony | ntp

Capability: ssh-server
Resolves-To: openssh-server

Capability: compiler-toolchain
Resolves-To: build-essential | gcc

Capability: vpn-client
Resolves-To: wireguard-tools

Capability: steam
Resolves-To: steam-installer | steam
